    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0487" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg475"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.111 Refugee Children/109</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Belgian Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Van der Straten-Ponthoz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="42" xml:id="d409-f1"/></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                        calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1942-10-05T23:59:59+02:00"
                        notBefore="1942-09-28T00:00:00+02:00">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">D. 8406</seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5955</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I understand that Your Excellency has
                    submitted to President Roosevelt a plan concerning the transfer to the United
                    States of four or five thousand children of different nationalities, such as
                    Belgians, Dutch, Czecoslovaquians and etc., who would remain in this country
                    until the end of hostilities.</p>
                <p>However, according to my information, the American Government wishes to obtain,
                    beforehand, from the interested governments, the assurance that these children
                    will be permitted to return to their respective countries after the war.</p>
                <p>As far as children sent from Belgium are concerned, I can give Your <pb
                        facs="0488" n="476" xml:id="pg476"/> Excellency assurances that Belgian
                    authorities will authorize the children of Belgian nationality to reenter
                    Belgium at the termination of their sojourn in the United States.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. v. Straten</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d409-f1" n="42" type="source" xml:id="d409-f1-content">
